From e0a63d287d60221deb605a2b4397d57119567cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:12:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(flowchart): square heads without moving the curve;
 stubs keep clear; wide strokes cut deeper (B1 review #1-#4, Q1+M1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Report §2.3; fixes the B1 review of fb3af47.

#1 (blocking) The arrow cut tilted heads wherever the drawn path's final
straight was shorter than the cut (subgraph.mmd routed C1/C2 -> Store,
0 -> 14.8 deg): the arc-length cut ended the stroke on the bend before it
and orient="auto" followed that. #2 (blocking) stubbed_cubic moved a
cubic's end point a head back, dragging its whole tail up to 9.5 px off
SceneEdge::bezier, against which routing, ports, labels and chips were
spaced (dense-td n16->n43 0.81 px off g10's chip, bench-75 casing gap
over svc4->cache's head, dense-lr overlaps).

Both replaced by one painter-only step, scene::square_end, run on every
glyph end of every drawn form (cubic, spline, mermaid curve) before the
cut: the end point stays put and the head faces the curve's own end
tangent. The curve's last stretch gives way to a straight run along that
tangent (up to a head, longest first) with a smooth bend into it, taken
only when the bend keeps within SQUARE_END_DEV (1 px) of the scene curve
outside the arrowhead. A curve too sharp for that (an S-cubic whose
handles are a fraction of its sideways reach: a wide fan's outer
branches turn 50-70 deg over their last head) enters the head straight
along a line touching it, onto a 1.5 px run past the cut: the head is
square, the tip on the border, and the stray (up to ~4 px) stays within
two heads of the tip. A mermaid `curve` only gets what its head needs.
drawn_segs (painter, picking, edge_end_tangent) = plain_segs + square_ends;
edge_distance squares an end only when the pointer is near a tip.
edge_painted_polyline keeps the scene curve's own samples up to the
junction. seg_param_at refines the cut within a sampled piece (was up to
0.1 px off on long cubics).

#3 edgepass::glyph_stubs (scene geometry for long edges) now weighs each
end's stub with stub_keeps_clear: rejected when the reshaped curve comes
nearer than CRAMP_NODE_GAP to an unrelated node than it was, or runs
longer within CLEAR_GAP / EDGE_SPACING of another edge (EDGE_SPACING only
for edges converging on the stubbed node). bench-75 static gw->svc5 keeps
its 16.6 px off lb: node_near 1 -> 0, defects 15 -> 13. Only the spline
spans near the change are sampled, so route() stays within budget.

#4 A linkStyle stroke wider than ARROW_TRIM stops its own width short
(arrow_trim = clamp(width, ARROW_TRIM, ARROW_MARKER_PX)), its head set
further ahead in an `<base>-t<width>` marker (arrow-t8, refX 2.727); the
advance painter keys its markers by colour and cut alike.

Corpus (14 flowcharts): heads <= 10 deg off square for non-bow ends
static 96.4% (pre-B1 91.1, fb3af47 98.8), routed 95.1% (94.7, 94.3 — the
criterion now met in both). Defects 69|98 = pre-B1 (fb3af47 72|99);
overlap 2746|7550 (fb3af47 3232|8414, pre 2764|7514), tight 9224|21070,
edge_chip routed 2. perf.sh within budget (bench-75 route 12.81 ms, drag
20.60 ms vs baseline 12.61 / 20.22).

Tests: new a_head_faces_the_end_tangent_where_the_final_straight_is_
shorter_than_the_cut (#1), squared_ends_face_the_curve_and_keep_near_it_
on_every_fixture (#1+#2, static and routed), a_turning_curve_runs_
straight_into_its_end_glyph_near_its_scene_curve (replaces a_turning_
cubic_runs_straight_into_its_end_glyph: no more stubbed_cubic),
a_wide_stroke_stops_its_width_short_under_its_own_head (#4),
edgepass a_stub_never_crowds_a_node_or_an_edge_its_curve_kept_clear_of
(#3). Changed: every_edge_kind_and_width_gets_one_head_size (a 6 px
stroke now gets arrow-t6, a 5 px one still shares #arrow);
class_and_er_edges_keep_their_painters_geometry (square_ends, not
glyph_stubs). Byte-exact diagrams_without_link_style_render_exactly_as_
before and edge_markers_draw_at_the_right_ends unchanged.

Gates (tests/quality.rs): the ones fb3af47 loosened are back at their
pre-B1 values — CHANNEL_MAX 2920|7620, 400|1290, 9350|21900, 3110|3700;
EDGE_CHIP_MAX (0, 2); GAP_FLOORS dense-lr 9.6, dense-td 12.1; dense-td
static ceiling 42. DEFECT_BASELINE (reasons in its comment): end_tilt
8 -> 14 static (the guard drops six stubs that crowded nodes or edges;
pre-B1 24), end_tilt_max routed 127.6 -> 128.4 (pre-B1: the bow's head
reads its uncut tangent), lat_backtrack routed 674 -> 676 and band_len
47754 -> 46610 routed (squared ends step sideways within their px),
band_pairs 119 -> 117, idiom_spline 27 -> 25, x_drawn 523 -> 521,
end_kink 19|39 -> 62|81 (fb3af47's low count came from the moved tails;
within a px of the scene curve, a curve swinging in from the side keeps
its kink at the head's base — squaring those needs the scene geometry).

Not done: #5 (heads touching at a 10 px port pitch on an over-full
side). Spilling ends round corners once the pitch drops under a head
(capacity at ARROW_MARKER_PX + 1) rerouted the dense fixtures (bench-75
routed end_tilt 16 -> 25, static defects 69 -> 72, edge_chip routed
2 -> 4): a ports-stage change (report §2.4), not B1.

